course: dictionary
lesson: 1472
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word and ask what the text is about. «A cataract is when the lens inside the eye becomes cloudy» is about the body, so here a cataract is a cloudy patch in the eye.
explain: Now read this: «The cataracts of the River Nile were rocky rapids that boats in ancient Egypt could not easily pass.» The clues are river, rocky and boats, so this cataract means a stretch of rough, rushing water. It is the same word with a different meaning, because the topic has changed.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. A cloudy waterfall or a rushing lens would not make sense, so the clues settle it.
fact: A cataract in the eye is a cloudy patch in the lens that makes things look blurry.
fact: Cataracts are common in older people, and a short operation can replace the cloudy lens with a clear plastic one.
fact: Cataracts are not catching; they don't spread like a cold.
fact: A cataract can also be a large, powerful waterfall or a stretch of rough, rushing water in a river.
fact: The cataracts of the Nile were rocky rapids that boats in ancient Egypt could not easily pass.
exercise: «A cataract is when the lens inside the eye becomes cloudy, usually with age.» What does cataract mean here? | A kind of cold that spreads quickly | A large, powerful waterfall | A plastic lens for a camera | *A cloudy patch in the lens of the eye
exercise: «The cataracts of the River Nile were rocky rapids that boats could not easily pass.» What does cataract mean here? | A type of boat | *A stretch of rough, rushing water | A cloudy patch in the eye | A rainy day at the seaside
exercise: Grandad says he will «have a cataract operation». What is the operation for? | To make a boat go faster | To move a river to a new place | *To replace a cloudy lens in the eye | To cure a bad cold
test: «An old dog's cloudy blue eyes often mean the lens has just hardened with age.» Why does the vet check the dog's eyes? | To see whether a cataract is blocking its sight | To find out if the dog likes the sea | *To check the dog's teeth | To measure how fast the dog can run
test: Which sentence uses cataract to mean a rushing waterfall? | «A cataract is when the lens inside the eye becomes cloudy.» | «Grandad will have a cataract surgery next week.» | «The vet checked the dog's blue eyes.» | *The cataracts of the Nile were rocky rapids that boats could not easily pass.
exam: What is the best way to work out the meaning of cataract in a new text? | Skip the word and never read the text again | Decide from how many letters the word has | Guess the first meaning you think of and never check it | *Read the clues around it, then check your meaning fits the sentence
